    exact_arms_attachment_is_zero: true
    weakly_identified_arms: ["cmr_only", "joint_exact_no_gauges", "joint_soft_attachment", "tee_only"]
    reproducibility_note: "An arm whose smallest non-gauge eigenvalue is far below the full model's sits in a nearly flat valley, so which point the regularizer settles on depends on floating-point rounding. Observed directly: across two machines the tee_only arm reproduced its held-out TEE error to 1e-13 but its held-out CMR extrapolation to only 1e-1. Cross-modal numbers from weakly identified arms should be read as indicative, not as reproducible measurements."
    interpretation_of_the_gauge_comparison: "A null result for full versus joint_exact_no_gauges on held-out error is the predicted outcome, not a failure. Theorem 3 concerns uniqueness of the identity/motion/session split conditional on the trajectories; removing the gauges leaves the trajectory space, and therefore the predictions, unchanged. What the gauges buy is visible in the alpha column instead: without them the identity and the common session mode trade off freely, so the arm's smallest non-gauge eigenvalue collapses to zero and the decomposition is unidentifiable even though it predicts just as well. That is the purpose the baseline lock assigns this arm, to test identifiability rather than generic fusion. Parameter recovery is measured separately in t3_gauge_ablation."
    gauges_are_necessary_for_identifiability: true
    soft_attachment_residual_is_nonzero: true
    total_failures: 0

